From d346798a54029f571e0e7ca12995ffbf975adac3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Advait Johari <zakethegr8@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:46:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] fix(windows): deliver explorer shortcuts in the
 background

Background hotkeys in File Explorer (Ctrl+Shift+N, Ctrl+X/V) reported
success and did nothing: the modifier-state technique only covered classic
windows, so Explorer's file view got a bare N/X/V.

hotkey and press_key now share post_key_background: post to the window
that has keyboard focus on the target's UI thread (Explorer's DirectUIHWND
or rename box), hold modifiers in that thread's key state until a WM_NULL
round trip shows the key was handled (120 ms floor), and return
background_unavailable when the key can't land (focus in an XAML island,
UIPI, attach failure, busy thread).

click with action "select" / "toggle" now pins that UIA pattern on any
window, so an Explorer file can be selected without being opened.
